# Force LF for every tracked file. actions/checkout defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows runners, which materialises Go sources as
# CRLF. gofmt wants LF-only, so the gofmt -l step then reports every .go
# file as unformatted. Pinning text=auto here overrides the local config.
* text=auto

# Go sources are the strictest case: gofmt compares byte-for-byte, so they
# must never be rewritten at checkout.
*.go text eol=lf

# Explicit text so line endings are normalised even for files with no other
# hint.
*.md text
*.yml text
*.yaml text
*.json text
*.mod text
*.sum text
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Local-only build scripts and data. eol=crlf keeps the committed
# build.bat double-quoted cmd syntax working if it is ever tracked.
Makefile text
config.example.json text eol=lf
